  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "Recent work supplies curated peptide solubility data and endpoint-specific ADMET protocols that enable controlled comparison of molecular property models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is controlled, protocol-matched evaluation of machine learning for molecular properties. PeptSol provides 1388 curated protected-peptide solubility measurements with chemistry-aware splits and evaluates seven frozen molecular encoders against them. Ark-ADMET treats representation and hyperparameter choice as endpoint-specific, reporting matches or gains over leaderboard scores on 7 of 21 endpoints under the TDC protocol. A separate immunogenicity study finds that a format lookup outperforms sequence predictors for ADA% labels, questioning the label basis itself. THEOBROMA contributes a different kind of resource: 1.13 million natural products with per-compound license auditing and stereochemistry-aware deduplication, relevant as curated input rather than as a model comparison.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
